# Twodos Slide — "Slide to Unlock": a horizontal iOS ScrollView with native rubber-band
# friction drives two rotating squares and a Skia squircle stroke that fills as the
# progress reaches 1 (haptic at >= 1, debounced).
# What this test covers: short drags right (partial stroke), long drags right
# past the unlock threshold (progress >= 1, haptic, stroke complete) and the
# bounce back; drags left (negative progress, squares rotate the other way
# through 0deg); flings both ways; grabbing the slider again during the
# bounce-back; repeated unlocks inside the 1s haptic debounce window.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/twodos-slide"
wait "text" "Slide to Unlock" 10000
wait 1000
gesture pan 120 560 60 0 600
wait 1000
gesture pan 60 560 300 0 1200
wait 1200
gesture pan 40 560 340 0 400
wait 1200
# Leftwards (negative progress).
gesture pan 360 560 -300 0 1200
wait 1200
gesture pan 380 560 -340 0 400
wait 1200
# Flings.
gesture fling right 120 560 250
wait 1000
gesture fling left 300 560 250
wait 1000
# Re-grab during bounce-back.
gesture pan 40 560 320 0 400
wait 150
gesture pan 100 560 250 0 500
wait 150
gesture pan 360 560 -300 0 400
wait 1200
# Repeated unlocks within the haptic debounce window.
gesture pan 40 560 340 0 300
wait 300
gesture pan 40 560 340 0 300
wait 300
gesture pan 40 560 340 0 300
wait 1500
wait "text" "Slide to Unlock" 3000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 3000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\" id=\"xmark\""
wait 1500
